  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GreenWizz</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2023 Greenwizz BV started developing energy solutions with a more direct climate impact. Currently Greenwizz BV is developing a rent-buy service for solar-panel installations in Ghana. The service aims to take away the biggest challenges for solar energy development in Ghana for small and medium enterprises (ME&#x2019;s) and institutes: 1. The upfront investment for a solar installation. 2. High quality material. 3. Technical expertise
Greenwizz BV takes care of upfront investment and installs the solar installation via a rent-buy agreement with the customer. This means the customer pays Greenwizz a monthly fee for a set period (e.g. 10 years) and after this period Greenwizz transfers the panels without additional costs to the company assuring a period of up to 20 years of free renewable electricity. 
During the rental period the aim is to keep the price at or below the grid price. In this way Greenwizz aims to create maximal local (climate and social) impact supplying reliable, renewable energy well below the market price (for the installation lifetime). At the same time there is strong focus on creating a healthy business performance for Greenwizz creating financial stability and allowing rapid growth of the project portfolio.
Greenwizz aims to primarily undertake projects involving 40-120 solar panels, though the company has the capability to manage larger projects through collaborations with external advisors. The focus is on delivering high-quality, standardized solar installations in partnership on equipment brands and types. They aim to avoid projects involving battery storage due to cost considerations, it can accommodate such needs in cases of high peak electricity usage, albeit with an adjusted risk fee.</narrative>
  </description>
